pan covers every component of the type in storage order, which is not the creation order once components were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"removed. It is zero copy: it views the storage itself. Because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~Escapable"},{"text":", it cannot leave ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(storing it in a variable outside the closure or returning it is a compile time error), so it can never dangle.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var maxX = 0","nexus.componentSpan(reading: Position.self) { (positions: Span<Position>) in","    for i in positions.indices { maxX = max(maxX, positions[i].x) }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"text":" is not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"},{"text":": loop over ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"indices"},{"text":". Element access is bounds checked.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs the type is locked for reading: structural changes (creating or destroying entities, adding or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"removing components, replacing a component with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":") and writes to the type stop the process with a message,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"since they would move or change what the span views. Reading the component through the nexus and reading","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the type again are fine. Collect changes and apply them after the call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An empty storage (or a type no entity ever had) passes an empty span.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Storage","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sparse-set storage keeps all components of a type in one array, so the span always views the storage itself.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The archetype storage keeps one column per table (one table per component set), so entities with different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component sets are not next to each other. If one table holds all components of the type the span views its column,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as above. If several tables hold them, the span views a temporary copy that is made table by table, which costs","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one allocation and O(N) copying per call and is released after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":". Use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to get zero copy spans, one batch per table."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1) plus ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)"]}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/Fir